v 3
d msat: treatment effects after endogenous switching regression
d
d msat is a post-estimation command for movestay (Lokshin and Sajaia 2004).
d It returns the four conditional expectations, the ATT, ATU and ATE with
d delta-method standard errors, the selection-on-gains parameter
d kappa = rho1*sigma1 - rho0*sigma0 with its Wald test, the expected-effect
d curves by quantile of a ranking variable, the marginal treatment effect
d with common-support flags, a two-step re-estimation of the model
d (twostep) and a semiparametric MTE by percentile-weights regression on
d the probit score (semipar). Survey weights (svyset) and household size
d are handled in every average.
d
d Requires: Stata 12 or later; movestay (ssc install movestay).
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260908
d Version: 1.3.1
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: abdelkrimaraar@gmail.com
d
